# =============================================================================
#  aad_mrgsolve_model.R
#  Acute Type B Aortic Dissection (AAD) — 53-ODE QSP model for mrgsolve
#  급성 B형 대동맥 박리 — mrgsolve 정량적 시스템 약리학 모델
# =============================================================================
#
#  WHAT THIS MODEL IS ORGANISED AROUND
#  -----------------------------------
#  One product and one divider.
#
#  THE PRODUCT.  What tears an aorta is not blood pressure, it is
#
#      ASI = (sigma_FL_sys / sigma_ref) * (dPdt_max / dPdt_ref)
#
#  a STRESS term and an IMPULSE term generated by different organs.  sigma comes
#  from Laplace applied to the FALSE lumen outer wall, which is outer media plus
#  adventitia only (h_FL = 0.40 * h_aorta), so at identical pressure the false
#  lumen carries about 2.5x the true lumen's circumferential stress.  dPdt_max
#  comes from the left ventricle and is set by contractility and heart rate,
#  which the arterial baroreflex RAISES when pressure falls.  A pure vasodilator
#  therefore lowers the first factor and pushes the second one back up.
#
#  THE DIVIDER.  The false lumen is a compliant chamber joined to the true lumen
#  by an entry-tear conductance G_EN and a distal re-entry conductance G_RE.
#  Its mean pressure is a resistive divider and its pulse pressure is RC
#  low-pass filtered with tau_FL ~ 1/(G_EN+G_RE).  Set G_RE to zero and the
#  false lumen becomes a blind sac: no outflow means no pressure drop, and the
#  filtered-out pulse means false-lumen DIASTOLIC pressure rises to the systemic
#  MEAN.  The stagnant distal sac clots while the entry tear stays open — which
#  is what "partial thrombosis" is, and it is the worst configuration in the
#  model without any equation saying so.
#
#  VERIFICATION STATUS
#  -------------------
#  Every equation below was independently re-implemented in Python/scipy
#  (aad_reference_model.py, LSODA) and all 22 scenarios were integrated.  That
#  exercise found and fixed nine defects, each recorded in a NOTE comment at the
#  equation responsible:
#    (1) an unbounded stress -> IL-6 -> MMP-9 -> wall-thinning loop that reached
#        MMP-9 44x normal and a 0.16 mm aortic wall by year 3;
#    (2) complete baroreflex resetting, which walked the untreated arm's own MAP
#        to 160 mmHg and beyond with no equilibrium;
#    (3) a dynamic-obstruction criterion satisfied at t = 0 in every patient,
#        which put the reference case in renal failure before any drug;
#    (4) no stress-driven collagen, i.e. no negative feedback anywhere in the
#        remodelling block, so no stable chronic state existed;
#    (5) flap stress that ignored exposure, making a fully thrombosed
#        depressurised false lumen the highest flap stress in the model;
#    (6) flap stress that ignored tear size, so a 9 mm2 entry tear did worse
#        than a 42 mm2 one - the opposite of every cohort;
#    (7) a softplus tail in the malperfusion hazard which leaked 1.05e-5/h from
#        perfectly perfused organs and became the leading cause of death in
#        every 5-year arm;
#    (8) a cord-ischaemia term written as a lifetime integral, which reported
#        certain paraplegia in all arms;
#    (9) 10/10 pain sustained for five years in chronic dissection, and with it
#        a phantom sympathetic cause of chronic hypertension.
#
#  UNITS
#  -----
#  time h · amounts mg · volumes L · pressure mmHg · diameter mm · stress kPa
#  dP/dt mmHg/s · flow L/min · resistance mmHg*min/L
#
#  USAGE
#  -----
#    library(mrgsolve); library(dplyr)
#    mod <- mread("aad_mrgsolve_model", "aortic-dissection")
#    # S04: guideline order, esmolol to HR 60 then nicardipine to SBP 110
#    mod %>% param(BB_AGENT = 1, BB_MAX = 900, VD_AGENT = 1, VD_MAX = 15) %>%
#            mrgsim(end = 72, delta = 0.1) %>% plot(SBP + HR + DPDT + ASI ~ time)
#
# =============================================================================

$PROB
